{"id":17444,"name":"Forsyth County","slug":"forsyth-county","state":"North Carolina","code":"NC","program":null,"sourceUrl":"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/tax-deed/tax-deed-states/north-carolina-tax-deed-sales/forsyth-county/","lastUpdated":"2026-07-20T14:51:10","facts":{"taxSaleType":"Tax Deed Sale","typicalSaleDate":"As needed, at 12:00 noon","bidProcedure":"Premium Bid","deposit":"5% – 20% of the highest bid​","extra":[{"label":"Auction Site","value":"175 N. Chestnut St, Winston-Salem, NC"},{"label":"Contact for More Information","value":"Tax Administration, Forsyth County"}]},"bodyHtml":"\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed aligncenter is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\n<span class=\"hTNsbyfgDP3eAIp3Hbga4mS8XDnL9kPhUqOjqWr5v9pIuzeAmREZM6GRx07O2VBYNv8LKw6QyWczodoV0kJ1rM4\"><iframe title=\"40-90% Savings on Real Estate - Forsyth County - North Carolina Tax Deed Investing\" width=\"1170\" height=\"658\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/pa7wiVN7E-c?feature=oembed\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen></iframe></span>\n</div></figure>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-16018d1d wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://linktr.ee/dustinhahnrealestateinvesting\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Click Here to Get Dustin Hahn’s Tax Lien and Deed FREE Mini-Course</a></div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">40-90% Savings on Real Estate &#8211; Forsyth County, North Carolina Tax Deed Investing</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Unlock massive savings on real estate in Forsyth County, North Carolina! Stay ahead of the game by doing your due diligence!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Forsyth County Tax Foreclosure Sale Information</h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Tax Foreclosure Sales</strong>: Sales are held at the Forsyth County Courthouse &#8211; 1st Floor, 175 N. Chestnut St., Winston-Salem, NC 27101​</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Sale Dates &amp; Times</strong>: Foreclosure sales occur as needed, typically at 12:00 noon. Keep an eye on the <a href=\"https://www.forsyth.cc/Tax/foreclosure_prop.aspx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Tax Administration page</mark></a> for the latest schedules​.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Payment Details</strong>: Be ready with 20% of your bid in cash, money orders, or certified funds at the time of the sale.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Upset Bids</strong>: After the sale, there’s a 10-day upset bid period where other interested parties can place higher bids. Stay alert during this time to ensure you remain the highest bidder​​.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Contact</strong>: For further inquiries, contact the Tax Administration at <a href=\"https://www.co.forsyth.nc.us/Tax/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Forsyth County Tax Administration</mark></a>​.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Important-Details-and-Links\">Important Details and Links</h4>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"></figure>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full\"><picture><source srcset=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Forsyth-County-Courthouse-Federal-Courthouse-Winston-Salem.webp 1081w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Forsyth-County-Courthouse-Federal-Courthouse-Winston-Salem-541x360.webp 541w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Forsyth-County-Courthouse-Federal-Courthouse-Winston-Salem-296x197.webp 296w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Forsyth-County-Courthouse-Federal-Courthouse-Winston-Salem-768x512.webp 768w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Forsyth-County-Courthouse-Federal-Courthouse-Winston-Salem-20x13.webp 20w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Forsyth-County-Courthouse-Federal-Courthouse-Winston-Salem-32x21.webp 32w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1081px) 100vw, 1081px\" type=\"image/webp\"><img src=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Forsyth-County-Courthouse-Federal-Courthouse-Winston-Salem.png\" height=\"720\" width=\"1081\" srcset=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Forsyth-County-Courthouse-Federal-Courthouse-Winston-Salem.png 1081w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Forsyth-County-Courthouse-Federal-Courthouse-Winston-Salem-541x360.png 541w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Forsyth-County-Courthouse-Federal-Courthouse-Winston-Salem-296x197.png 296w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Forsyth-County-Courthouse-Federal-Courthouse-Winston-Salem-768x512.png 768w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Forsyth-County-Courthouse-Federal-Courthouse-Winston-Salem-20x13.png 20w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Forsyth-County-Courthouse-Federal-Courthouse-Winston-Salem-32x21.png 32w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1081px) 100vw, 1081px\" class=\"wp-image-17450 sp-no-webp\" alt=\"Forsyth County Courthouse Federal Courthouse Winston-Salem\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"  > </picture></figure>\n</div>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Pro Tips</h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Stay Updated</strong>: Regularly check the Forsyth County Tax Administration website for the latest updates on foreclosure sales.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Understand the Upset Bid Process</strong>: Prepare for the 10-day upset bid period. This is a crucial time to ensure you remain the highest bidder.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Do Your Homework</strong>: These properties come with no guarantees. Inspect them thoroughly before placing your bid​​.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">FAQs</h3>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Can I purchase tax lien certificates in Forsyth County?</strong> </p>\n\n\n\n<p>No, North Carolina law prohibits the sale of property tax liens​.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>What type of payment is accepted for the deposit?</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<p>You can make deposits using cash, money orders, or certified funds. Checks should be payable to Zacchaeus Legal Services​​.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Where do I place an upset bid?</strong> Submit upset bids in person at the Clerk of Court’s Office, Room #4501, Hall of Justice, 175 N. Chestnut St, Winston-Salem, NC​​.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>What happens if no one places an opening bid at a foreclosure sale?</strong> </p>\n\n\n\n<p>Properties that don&#8217;t receive an initial bid enter Foreclosure Sale Residual Parcel status and may be auctioned again later​.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Useful Links</h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><a href=\"https://www.co.forsyth.nc.us/Tax/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Forsyth County Tax Administration</mark></a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://www.forsyth.cc/Tax/foreclosure_prop.aspx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Foreclosure Sales Information</mark></a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/tax-deed/tax-deed-states/north-carolina-tax-deed-sales/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">How to Unlock Profits and Secure Real Estate Deals in North Carolina Tax Deeds</mark></a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/tax-deed/tax-deed-investing-overview/understanding-tax-deed-investing/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Let’s talk about Tax Deeds and how you can profit from them!</mark></a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://youtu.be/ES5ZPyHRFMM?si=EmzhADUvwB_2FAAr\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Discover Tax Deeds and how you can find property for as little as $50!&nbsp;</mark></a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://youtu.be/y6XF52gRsLY?si=O9d1jUv2NeJxjyvY\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">This is how you can get properties below market value in North Carolina!</mark></a></li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Need a Hand?</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>If you need assistance or guidance with tax lien investing, feel free to reach out for help. You can <a href=\"https://linktr.ee/dustinhahnrealestateinvesting\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">book a call</mark></a> or access <a href=\"https://linktr.ee/dustinhahnrealestateinvesting\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">free resources</mark></a> to get started on your investment journey.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Remember, thorough research and preparation can lead to significan